  "chain": "steam leak near TSV-4 limit switch [cause B] -> elevated temperature degrades switch shaft/bearing lubricant -> shaft binds in actuated position -> limit switch fails to actuate on TSV-4 closure -> RPS channel A2 & one EOC-RPT channel inoperable beyond TS completion time [backup: redundant B2/other channels remained OPERABLE]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Recurring failure mode across multiple LaSalle TSV limit switches (2019, 2019, 2022 Unit1, 2022 Unit2) all tied to lubricant degradation from heat exposure; this event's steam leak specifically circumvented prior corrective actions (high-temp switches, housing mods). RPS and EOC-RPT modeled as non-EIIS Systems since they are the affected safety functions, not the failed component's EIIS system (TA/main turbine). Redundant B2 channel and other TSV channels remained OPERABLE, but narrative doesn't name a distinct backup System node to attach BACKED_UP_BY to beyond noting redundancy in the consequence description."
}